# Round mtpcost: the MTP arm's prompt warmup walks the draft's store through the wide launches the
# ubatch walk runs (mtp38 store_walk: the pack and the attention site's mix quantized to 32-value q8
# blocks, eh_proj, q, k and v as 32-value GEMMs, one walk of up to MTP_STORE_ROWS = 64 rows) instead
# of 8-row walks of the m-column gemvs. Same binary, two arms by the draft lever, as the mtppf
# window (docs/cards/mtppf-pp.card; its log: plain pp512 618.60 / pp4096 614.74, mtp 573.15 /
# 556.10 tok/s, 3 rounds, prose, A6000 plan a, C 4352).
# Decomposing that window's gap at P 4096, per round from its `stat prompt host` and `time prompt`
# rows: the plain wall 6,663 ms; the mtp arm's 7,365 ms; the union term (the draft's card reserve)
# +377..+422 ms; the rest, ~300 ms over 513 store walks of up to 8 rows, 0.585 ms a walk (0.55 at P
# 512, 65 walks). Per walk the DRAM bytes are ~95 MB (0.14 ms at 700 GB/s) and the FP32 FMAs ~0.69 G
# (~40 us); what the bytes do not explain is the gemvs' f32 activations, re-read by every weight row
# (eh_proj 2,560 rows x 32 columns x 5,120 values = 1.68 GB of L1/L2 requests a walk, q 1.0 GB),
# and the sub-wave launches (k and v 64 blocks, the mix, the embedding, the pack, the append).
# The wide walk reads each weight once per 64 rows and stages the activations as int8 in shared
# memory: per 64-row walk, 19 launches, ~55 MB of weights, 11 G int8 MACs; the sub-wave terms are
# the mix's down GEMM (3 blocks of 128 rows at K 10,240) and the k and v GEMMs (4 blocks each):
# 0.2-0.45 ms a walk [derived], 64 walks at P 4096: 13-29 ms; 8 walks at P 512: 1.6-3.6 ms. The
# arena grows 24,877,352 B (place.rs mtp_arena_bytes), 6 target experts off the card at this
# placement [derived, the qwen4exp_meta replica: 11,925 -> 11,919 at A6000 4k U 4,096], +~500 host
# slots and +3 ms of union at P 4096.
# This card needs the app's warmup to chunk by MTP_STORE_ROWS (crates/app/src/arch/qwen3moe/mod.rs
# `warm`); with the app still chunking by 8 rows the walk is 8 rows wide and this band does not apply.
# New MTP arm [derived]: P 4096 6,663 + 330..440 + 3 + 13..29 = 7,009..7,135 ms against 6,663:
# -6.6..-4.9 %; P 512 828 + 27..35 + 1.6..3.6 = 857..867 ms: -4.5..-3.4 % (printed, not decided).
# The runner (wall: the mtppf window took ~6 min for the same 12 processes):
# BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/mtpcost-pp.card BLOOMERY_GEN_CTX=4352' BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=3
# just depth-gpu-qwen4exp prose:512 prose:512@BLOOMERY_DRAFT=mtp prose:4096 prose:4096@BLOOMERY_DRAFT=mtp
kind: ab
question: does walking the draft's prompt warmup through the wide store walk close the MTP arm's
  prompt gap down to the draft's card reserve, as the wide walk's launch and GEMM costs predict?
term: pp tok/s @ P=4096 (prose:4096, the time prompt row), n=96, ctx 4352 (BLOOMERY_GEN_CTX=4352),
  A6000, plan a (card experts), BLOOMERY_DRAFT=mtp against unset, same binary, paired by round
unit: %
predict: -6.6..-4.9
rounds: 3
sd: 0.55 % the q38mtp-tg sitting's pp4096 rows (docs/cards/q38mtp-tg.card), plain/mtp paired ratio
  SD 0.75 % over 3 rounds, divided by the square root of 2
condition: one binary, both arms of a P in one lease, a fresh process per load group, the host set
  and the PLE table warm (majflt near 0), no [cpu-busy] or [other-busy] row; the mtp arm's load line
  names draft=mtp and head=full and its arena=51,148,972 (the mtppf window's 26,271,620 plus the
  store arena's 24,877,352); each arm's stat prompt host line gives host_slots 908,274 (plain) and
  981,105 + 200..900 (mtp) at P 4096, 115,726 and 123,608 + 20..120 at P 512; the store the warmup
  leaves reads as before: the mtp arm's decode at prose:512 near the mtppf window's 80.2 tok/s (a
  store off by more than its q8 band drops the acceptance toward the plain 52.8) and each arm's
  distinct_tokens the plain arm's (70 at P 512, 61 at P 4096)
decide-in: land mtpcost with the app's chunk edit; the prompt gap left is the draft's card reserve
  (94 % of it the draft's 512 Q8_0 experts, 2.67 GB), and the MTP default is decided on decode
  +31..+52 % against this pp
decide-below: the wide walk costs more than 0.45 ms or a term outside it moved: read each arm's stat
  prompt host union_ms first (+330..+440 ms at P 4096); inside that band, nsys one MTP prompt call at
  P 4096 and read the store walks' per-launch durations (the mix's down GEMM, k and v) before any
  change
decide-above: the union term landed under +330 ms or the warmup under 13 ms: compare both arms'
  host_slots and union_ms with this card's, then re-derive the union's share from one
  BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1 run before the next round
